ikal","gloss":"day"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"every"}],"gloss":"every day"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடுகொளக்","parts":[{"text":"ஆடுகொளக்","lemma":"ஆடுகொளக்","gloss":"to attain victory"}],"gloss":"to attain victory","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குழைந்த","parts":[{"text":"குழை","lemma":"kuḻai","gloss":"wither"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"nt","gloss":"past tense infix"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"tt","gloss":"euphonic"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"withered"},{"surface":"தும்பைப்","parts":[{"text":"தும்பைப்","lemma":"தும்பைப்","gloss":"tumpai flower"}],"gloss":"tumpai flower","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"pulavar","gloss":"poets"}],"gloss":"poets"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடுதுறை","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"singing"},{"text":"துறை","lemma":"tuṟai","gloss":"theme"}],"gloss":"themes of song"},{"surface":"முற்றிய","parts":[{"text":"முற்றிய","lemma":"முற்றிய","gloss":"who mastered"}],"gloss":"who mastered","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொற்ற","parts":[{"text":"கொற்ற","lemma":"கொற்ற","gloss":"victorious"}],"gloss":"victorious","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேந்தே","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தே","lemma":"வேந்தே","gloss":"O King!"}],"gloss":"O King!","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இகழுநர்","parts":[{"text":"இகழ்","lemma":"ikaḻ","gloss":"oppose"},{"text":"உநர்","lemma":"unar","gloss":"they who"}],"gloss":"those who oppose you"},{"surface":"இசையடு","parts":[{"text":"இசையடு","lemma":"இசையடு","gloss":"along with their fame"}],"gloss":"along with their fame","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாயப்","parts":[{"text":"மாயப்","lemma":"மாயப்","gloss":"to perish"}],"gloss":"to perish","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புகழொடு","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"pukaḻ","gloss":"fame"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with fame"},{"surface":"விளங்கிப்","parts":[{"text":"விளங்கிப்","lemma":"விளங்கிப்","gloss":"shining"}],"gloss":"shining","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பூக்க","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"pū","gloss":"bloom"},{"text":"க","lemma":"ka","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may it bloom"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"வேலே","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"spear!"}]}],"literal":"O Lord abundant in fame, transcending the limit of scholars! / The deep-placed moat that transcended the earth's boundary, / The fortress wall touching the sky, / The beautiful defense ports like stars blossomed in the sky, / The protected forest barrier dense with trees where sun rays cannot enter, / The fortress of Kāṉappēr surrounded by difficult strongholds, / The red fire kindled by the strong-handed blacksmith / Consuming water, saying it is impossible to retrieve, / While Vēṅkaimārpaṉ laments every day, / With withered tumpai flowers worn by poets to attain victory, / O victorious King who mastered the themes of song! / May those who oppose you perish along with their fame, / And may your spear bloom, shining with fame!","translation":"O Lord of abundant fame, whose greatness exceeds the praise of scholars! The fortress of Kāṉappēr was surrounded by difficult strongholds, with a deep moat that seemed to reach the very bottom of the earth, a sky-touching wall, beautiful defense ports resembling stars blooming in the sky, and a dense, protective forest barrier where even the sun's rays could not enter. Just as water swallowed by the red-hot iron in a strong-handed blacksmith's fire can never be recovered, the defeated king Vēṅkaimārpaṉ laments every day, knowing his lost fort can never be retrieved. O victorious King, who has mastered all the themes sung by poets wearing withered tumpai flowers of victory! May those who despise you perish along with their fame, and may your spear ever shine and bloom with glory!","modern":"புலவர்களின் புகழுக்கும் அப்பாற்பட்ட, பெரும் புகழுடைய தலைவனே! பூமியின் எல்லையைக் கடந்து ஆழமாக அமைந்த அகழியும், வானத்தைத் தொடுவது போன்ற மதிலும், வானத்தில் பூத்த விண்மீன்களைப் போன்ற அழகிய ஞாயில்களும், சூரியனின் கதிர்களும் நுழைய முடியாதபடி மரங்கள் அடர்ந்த காவல் காடும் ஆகியவற்றைக்கொண்டு, பகைவர் கடப்பதற்கரிய அரண்களால் சூழப்பட்டிருந்தது கானப்பேரெயில் என்னும் கோட்டை. வலிமையான கைகளையுடைய கொல்லன் மூட்டிய செந்தீயில் சூடேறிய இரும்பு உறிஞ்சிய நீரை மீண்டும் பெற முடியாது. அதுபோல, உன்னால் கைப்பற்றப்பட்ட அக்கோட்டையை மீண்டும் மீட்பது இயலாது என்று எண்ணி, வேங்கைமார்பன் என்னும் மன்னன் தன் நெஞ்சு வருந்தி நாள்தோறும் அழுகிறான். வெற்றி பெறுவதற்காகத் தும்பைப்பூவைச் சூடிப் போரிட்டு, வாடிய தும்பை மாலையோடு விளங்கும் வீரர்களைப் பாடும் புலவர்களின் பாடுதுறைகள் அனைத்தையும் முழுமையாக உணர்ந்த வெற்றி வேந்தனே! உன்னை இகழ்ந்து பேசும் பகைவர்கள் தங்கள் புகழோடு அழியட்டும்! உன்னுடைய வேல் புகழோடு விளங்கி எப்போதும் வெற்றிப் பூக்களைச் சூடட்டும்!","explanation":"The poet Aiyūr Mūlaṅkiḻār sings in praise of the Pāṇṭiya king Ukkirap Peruvaḻuti, who successfully captured the formidable fortress of Kāṉappēreyil from the chieftain Vēṅkaimārpaṉ. The poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai (victory), specifically the Arasavākai theme, which celebrates the military triumph and royal greatness of a king. The poet vividly describes the impregnable nature of the Kāṉappēr fortress, with its deep moat, high walls, star-like defense ports, and dense protective forest. He uses a striking simile: just as water absorbed by red-hot iron in a blacksmith's forge can never be recovered, the lost fortress can never be reclaimed by its former ruler, who now laments daily. The poet concludes by wishing that the king's enemies perish in ignominy while the king's victorious spear continues to shine with eternal glory.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}